//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// HOW LOOT ACTUALLY SPAWNS INSIDE BUILDS
//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

/*
IMPORTANT TRUTH:

mapgroupproto DOES NOT spawn loot.

It only spawns OBJECTS.

Loot comes from:

1. types.xml (item definitions)
2. class names inside containers
3. Central Economy spawn rules
*/



//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// HOW TO TURN A BUILD INTO A LOOT ZONE
//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

STEP 1: Place containers in mapgroupproto

<group name="LootCamp">

    <child name="Land_WoodenCrate" pos="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0" />
    <child name="Land_SeaChest" pos="2 0 0" rpy="0 0 0" />
    <child name="Land_MetalCrate" pos="-2 0 0" rpy="0 0 0" />

</group>



STEP 2: Place group in world

<group name="LootCamp" pos="6100 9000" />



STEP 3: Ensure loot is enabled in types.xml

Example:

<class name="WoodenCrate">
    <nominal>10</nominal>
    <min>5</min>
    <lifetime>3600</lifetime>
</class>



RESULT:

- crates spawn via mapgroupproto
- crates fill via CE loot system
- players loot crates naturally



